tHash":"7a82e267-f0df-4ecd-87a5-12b1c99395a9"},{"objectId":"5e7092a2878c28a047399adb","name":"Zbigniew","lastName":"Jachna","uuid":"66D254C2F8ACD65A9982EA214B06261952B6C282CCCB0642FE34781CD8E7AAFCF8CC0CCA8D3C71761BA0D1E5BB499BA0AEE22CE1E259701447A790A07E9A577B","orcidId":"0000-0003-4382-3325","documentHash":"265e497e-2b60-4ea1-824e-18a744fd2b4c"}],"openAccess":{"textVersion":"FINAL_PUBLISHED","license":"CC_BY_NC_ND","releaseDate":"2025-09-18","releaseDateMode":"AT_PUBLICATION","mode":"OPEN_JOURNAL"},"objectId":"692d7988fdbe831c4a49cc38","doi":"10.24425/mms.2025.155804","publicUri":"https://journals.pan.pl/dlibra/publication/155804/edition/137338/content","type":"ARTICLE","typeName":"Artykuł","year":2025,"title":"High-precision 3-channel time interval counter in a low-cost AMD Spartan-7 FPGA","otherTitles":[],"abstracts":[{"languageCode":"eng","content":"This paper presents the design, implementation, and performance evaluation of a 3-channel integrated time interval counter implemented in a low-cost Spartan-7 (AMD/Xilinx) FPGA device. Based on a hybrid measurement approach that combines timestamping and two-stage interpolation, the proposed solution provides high metrological parameters, such as: time resolution (2 ps), measurement precision (better than 8 ps) and range (up to 1 h). To achieve high resolution and reduce nonlinearity of the time-to-digital converters (TDCs) involved, the multi-edge coding in four independent tapped delay lines (TDL) was applied. An improved encoder eliminates bubble errors and compresses raw TDL data with limited logic overhead.\nThe integrated code processor performs real-time calibration based on the statistical code density test (SCDT). Implemented within a low-end FPGA chip, the time counter occupies approximately one-third of available logic resources and consumes around 0.5 W. Experimental evaluation confirms the system’s potential for cost-effective, high-performance time interval measurements in portable instrumentation."}],"